{:edb/db-before-t 2030 :edb/db-after-t 2031 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535343 50 #inst "2026-10-08T22:29:34.905Z" 13194139535343 true] [17592186087702 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344803 13194139535343 true] [17592186087702 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344810 13194139535343 true] [17592186087702 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344855 13194139535343 true] [17592186087702 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344891 13194139535343 true] [17592186087703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344845 13194139535343 true] [17592186087703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344850 13194139535343 true] [17592186087703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344863 13194139535343 true] [17592186087703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344870 13194139535343 true] [17592186087703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344898 13194139535343 true] [17592186087737 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344824 13194139535343 true] [17592186087737 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344831 13194139535343 true] [17592186087737 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344838 13194139535343 true] [17592186087738 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344817 13194139535343 true] [17592186087738 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344860 13194139535343 true] [17592186087738 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344877 13194139535343 true] [17592186087738 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344884 13194139535343 true] [17592186088078 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535343 true] [17592186088078 1100 "The position vector $r$, in meters, of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$r = ⟨4t^{3/2} + 4t^{2} + 5, t^{3} - 4t^{2} + t⟩, t > 0$.\nCalculate the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t = 1$." 13194139535343 false] [17592186088078 1100 "The position vector $r,$ in meters, of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨4{t}^{3/2}+4{t}^{2}+5,\\,{t}^{3}-4{t}^{2}+t⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=1.$" 13194139535343 true] [17592186088078 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3/2}+4{t}^{2}+5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-4{t}^{2}+t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6{t}^{1/2}+8t,\\,3{t}^{2}-8t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{1/2}+8t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-8t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{-1/2}+8,\\,6t-8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨3(1)^{-1/2}+8,\\,6(1)-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3+8,\\,6-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨11,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(1)|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(1)| & =|⟨11,\\,-2⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{11}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{125} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535343 true] [17592186088164 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535343 true] [17592186088164 1100 "The velocity vector $v = ⟨u, v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$v = ⟨3t^{3},-\\frac{1}{2}t^{2}⟩$.\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t = 3$." 13194139535343 false] [17592186088164 1100 "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨3{t}^{3},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=3.$" 13194139535343 true] [17592186088164 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9{t}^{2},\\,-t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=3,$ we substitute $t=3$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(3) & =⟨9(3)^{2},\\,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9\\cdot 9,\\,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨81,\\,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344803 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344804 13194139535343 true] [17592186344803 1089 "q-121903" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344803 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535343 true] [17592186344803 1100 "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t+2),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+5)⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a.$" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344803 1113 #uuid "43a48947-068a-5638-90e7-fa84c34661dc" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344803 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t+2)),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+5))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{3t+2},2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+5)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344805 13194139535343 true] [17592186344804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344806 13194139535343 true] [17592186344804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344807 13194139535343 true] [17592186344804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344808 13194139535343 true] [17592186344804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344809 13194139535343 true] [17592186344804 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535343 true] [17592186344804 1041 "selection" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344804 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344807 13194139535343 true] [17592186344804 1110 #uuid "7ab2f0fd-c1cd-5c59-862d-73cd691950d1" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344805 1034 "a=⟨\\frac{3}{3t+2},-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+5)⟩" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344805 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194