"To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-3{t}^{2}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨15{t}^{2}-4t,\\,4{t}^{3}-6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(15{t}^{2}-4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-6t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨30t-4,\\,12{t}^{2}-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2) & =⟨30(2)-4,\\,12(2)^{2}-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨60-4,\\,48-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨56,\\,42⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(2)|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(2)| & =|⟨56,\\,42⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{56}^{2}+{42}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3136+1764} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4900} \\\\  & =70\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the acceleration at time $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is $70{\\text{ m/s}}^{2}.$" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344862 13194139535343 true] [17592186344861 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535343 true] [17592186344861 1041 "field-1" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344861 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344862 13194139535343 true] [17592186344861 1110 #uuid "38b0a552-615b-5d02-8c6a-fe487a7924e7" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344862 1034 "70" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344862 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535343 true] [17592186344862 1111 #uuid "99d59a7d-7210-5e4d-88e4-11b81e7493aa" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344863 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344864 13194