lculate the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=1.$" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344884 1113 #uuid "4a4780c3-0145-50d6-a5b4-086eefdf5f1d" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344884 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4}{1+t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-4t+5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{(1+t)^{2}},\\,{t}^{2}-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{4}{(1+t)^{2}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{8}{(1+t)^{3}},\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨\\frac{8}{(1+(1))^{3}},\\,2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{8}{{2}^{3}},\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(1)|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(1)| & =|⟨1,\\,2⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344886 13194139535343 true] [17592186344885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344887 13194139535343 true] [17592186344885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344888 13194139535343 true] [17592186344885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344889 13194139535343 true] [17592186344885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344890 13194139535343 true] [17592186344885 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535343 true] [17592186344885 1041 "selection" 13194139535343 true] [17592186344885 1104 